@startuml
title TurboWin+ CI tasks (GitHub Actions and GitLab)
start
if (Manual JAR request?) then (yes)
  :Linux amd64 / Java 21;
  :task_linux.bash jar;
  :Upload build/libs/;
else (push / pull request)
  fork
    :Linux amd64 test job;
    :Install X11 / Openbox / ffmpeg;
    :Wait for Xvfb readiness;
    :Start window manager and recording;
    :Gradle test --no-daemon\n10-minute timeout + kill grace;
    :Cleanup desktop / finalize recording\nPreserve test exit status;
    :Attempt test artifact upload\nalso after failure;
    note right
      GitHub: 20-minute job limit;
      video, log, HTML and XML reports.
      GitLab: video artifact; retry 2.
      Upload only files actually produced.
    end note
  fork again
    :Linux amd64 DEB;
    :task_linux.bash deb\njlink + jpackage;
    :Upload build/jpackage/;
  fork again
    :Linux ARM64 DEB;
    :task_linux.bash deb\njlink + jpackage;
    :Upload build/jpackage/;
  fork again
    :Linux amd64 RPM;
    :task_linux.bash rpm\njlink + jpackage;
    :Upload build/jpackage/;
  fork again
    :Windows x64 EXE;
    :task_windows.ps1\nDownload JDK / WiX\njlink + jpackage;
    :Upload build/jpackage/;
  end fork
endif
note right
  GitHub: separate workflows; JAR uses workflow_dispatch.
  GitLab: one build stage; JAR is manual.
  Email build settings required; dummy fallbacks only in GitHub test.
  No signing or release-publication stage is implemented.
end note
stop
@enduml
